    Vendor HAL framework compatibility matrix — level-less.
    Generated iter 216 from check_vintf_compatible error output.
    
    Key architectural insight (VintfObject.cpp:1370):
    Matrices WITHOUT a level attribute are SKIPPED by
    checkMatrixHalsHasDefinition (the "Typo?" source-definition check).
    But check_vintf_compatible DOES read their HAL entries.
    
    So: level-less matrix with vendor HAL entries satisfies
    check_vintf_compatible (vendor HALs are declared) WITHOUT
    triggering check_vintf_system (no source-definition validation).
    FCM level comes from AOSP compatibility_matrix.202504.xml.
    
    All entries are AIDL format, optional=true (vendor-to-vendor services).
-->
